umer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 49%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $38K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Carvana Co. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $160.4B market cap on $20.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 26% against a 12% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 14% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $889M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.74\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.7\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 0.3% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 2.0% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 298% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.9827807718293813},{"text":"Beneish M-Score flags potential earnings manipulation \u2014 a question of whether the reported numbers can be trusted","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $12.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 5% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Here is What to Know Beyond Why Carvana Co. (CVNA) is a Trending Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3032314/here-is-what-to-know-beyond-why-carvana-co-cvna-is-a-trending-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cmost_searched_stocks_v1-3032314","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795093203.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (CVNA) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/90/The_Technic